                                                "example_id": "032a22c4-b18e-42c0-b631-2c05a0894b13",
                                                "sense_id": "59c47e25-eedc-3d95-a9a1-6089541af69d",
                                                "text": "next friend"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7edce74-0b11-40fd-8c21-a069b1394732",
                                                "sense_id": "59c47e25-eedc-3d95-a9a1-6089541af69d",
                                                "text": "And if a man purchase land in fee simple and die without issue, he which is his next cousin collaterall of the whole blood, how farre so ever he be from him in degree, (de quel pluis long degree qu'il soit), may inherite and have the land ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c1e176b-d61c-48bb-bb99-47153b106949",
                                                "sense_id": "59c47e25-eedc-3d95-a9a1-6089541af69d",
                                                "text": "Thomas Humphrey Doleman died the 30th of August 1712, an infant, intestate and without issue; Lewis the next nephew died the 17th of April 1716, an infant about sixteen years old, having left his mother Mary Webb, ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25e2c285-b2d7-4ed5-abe9-143f2e9acff1",
                                                "sense_id": "59c47e25-eedc-3d95-a9a1-6089541af69d",
                                                "text": "If it be a property, it is a new species, unknown to the civil law, the common law, and the statute law; there is no medium, it must be, if it goes to her next kin, because it is absolute property in her. There can be no distribution of personal property ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
